    "Figure_4_binary_morphology_roc": {
      "caption": "Figure 4. Exploratory binary morphology ROC curves for the primary YOLO11l-cls model (seed 0): (A) internal validation and (B) external test. The positive group combines parasyndesmophytes and syndesmophytes; the negative group combines normal morphology and osteophytes. The score is P(parasyndesmophytes) + P(syndesmophytes). Orange diamonds indicate the threshold 0.271, selected by maximizing Youden's index in internal validation and applied unchanged externally; the full-precision value is in the deposited validation_selected_threshold.json. Insets display the same curves over false-positive rates 0.00-0.20 and true-positive rates 0.80-1.00; dashed rectangles mark those regions in the full-scale plots. Confidence intervals for AUC are the saved 2000-replicate image-level bootstrap intervals. Operating-point uncertainty does not include uncertainty in selecting the validation threshold. This grouping concerns radiographic morphology and is not a clinical diagnosis of axial spondyloarthritis.",
